<title>UK: EIB sets 70 bln yen April 2000 dual-currency bond.</title>
<headline>EIB sets 70 bln yen April 2000 dual-currency bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following dual-currency Samurai bond was announced by lead manager Yamaichi Securities.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EUROPEAN INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT    70 BLN YEN    COUPON     5.05	MATURITY    28.APR.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    31.OCT.96</p>
<p>FULL FEES  1.50</p>
<p> NOTES	REDEMPTION IN US DOLLARS</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    =	   PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) =	   SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.25	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	EXCHANGE RATE AT REDEMPTION IS 500,000YEN/$4,468.27</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
